      "side": 1,
      "message": "`VALI_NO_OPT` (`optimising()`) changes the artifact but is in neither the stamp nor the key, so the two settings share one entry and the first run decides what both get.\n\n- A cold `VALI_NO_OPT\u003d1` run of a small library writes a 904-byte entry.\n- A cold optimised run on an empty cache writes 907 bytes at the same path.\n- Each later run, in either mode, loads whichever is there.\n\nSo `VALI_NO_OPT\u003d1`, which exists to bypass the optimiser, silently runs optimised code for cached libraries, and the reverse. It also makes ADR line 91\u0027s \"they compile the same bytes\" untrue for two concurrent runs.\n\nHash the setting into the stamp (or the key), or skip the cache when it\u0027s set.",
      "revId": "b401f85c030810abf9c75a1534042d3d51ed55c7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
