      "side": 1,
      "message": "This takes any `*.vac` or `.tmp-*` file in any subdirectory of the root as an entry, and `remove_empty_dirs` (line 320) removes every empty subdirectory, not just stamp directories.\n\nWith a root holding `notes/design.vac`, `notes/readme.txt`, `build/.tmp-session` and an empty `emptydir/`, `vali --cache-dir D cache clean` leaves only `notes/readme.txt`. `prune` matches the same files.\n\nThat contradicts 1260917\u0027s ADR text (\"Only files the cache itself names are ever deleted, so a directory that holds other things is safe to point it at\"), and `--cache-dir`/`VALI_CACHE_DIR` invite pointing it at a project directory.\n\nMatch only what `entry` and the temp writer make: directories named with 16 hex digits, files named `\u003c64 hex\u003e.vac` or the exact temp pattern. And only remove those directories.",
      "revId": "b401f85c030810abf9c75a1534042d3d51ed55c7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
